<title>SOUTH AFRICA: Corwil lifts yr shr earnings, no div.</title>
<headline>Corwil lifts yr shr earnings, no div.</headline>
<dateline>JOHANNESBURG 1997-06-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>Preliminary profit statement for the year ended March 31 1997.</p>
<p>			(million rand unless stated)</p>
<p>Shr, (cts)</p>
<p>    - attrib		  21.3	  vs   15.0</p>
<p>    Div (cts)		  -	    vs    9.0</p>
<p>Income after</p>
<p>    income tax		 0.40	 vs    0.28</p>
<p>    Pre-tax		    0.42	 vs    0.29</p>
<p>    Tax			  0.02	 vs    0.01</p>
<p>    Interest paid	    0.05	 vs    0.03</p>
<p>    Income		     0.50	 vs    0.39</p>
<p>Full name: Corwil Investments Limited</p>
<p>NOTE - Directors advised that it was their intention to increase the authorised share capital of the company to create an executive share trust. In addition they would request members to place the unissued shares under the control of the directors and give the directors the authority to issue these shares for cash as and when suitable situations arose.</p>
<p>Shareholders would be advised of the terms and conditions of the above when the annual report was issued in July 1996.</p>
<p>-- Johannesburg newsroom 27 11 482 1003</p>
</text>
